    "final_text": "I added `updateQuantity(name, quantity)` to `ShoppingCart` in `src/cart.js`, and the full suite passes (69 tests, 0 failures).\n\n- **Validation:** a quantity that isn't a non-negative integer throws a `RangeError`. That includes `NaN`, `Infinity`, strings, `null` and `undefined`. `RangeError` is a subclass of `Error` and matches what `addItem` throws. A name that isn't in the cart throws a plain `Error`, the same as `removeItem`.\n- **Order of checks:** validation runs before anything changes, so a rejected call leaves the cart as it was.\n- **Behaviour:** a quantity of 0 removes the item, and any other valid quantity replaces the existing one.\n\nI added an `updateQuantity` block to `tests/cart.test.js`. It covers:\n- raising and lowering a quantity\n- removal at 0\n- each bad quantity type\n- a missing item\n- a missing item combined with a bad quantity\n\nThe rejection tests check that the cart is unchanged afterwards.\n\nI briefly added a stray placeholder test to the test file by mistake, then removed it before writing the real tests.",
